      "tool": "Kinetics",
      "text": "Michaelis–Menten enzyme kinetics\n\nE + S ⇌ ES → E + P with k1 = 10, k−1 = 1, kcat = 2 and [E]0 = 0.01: the initial velocities at six substrate concentrations follow the hyperbola v = Vmax·S / (KM + S), and the Lineweaver–Burk plot recovers KM and Vmax.\n\nNetwork:\nE = 0.01\nS = 2\nES = 0\nP = 0\nE + S <=> ES ; kf = 10, kr = 1\nES -> E + P ; k = 2\nMichaelis–Menten (E + S ⇌ ES → E + P): KM = (k−1 + kcat)/k1 = 0.3, Vmax = kcat[E]0 = 0.02.\nInitial velocities: S = 0.1: v = 0.005; S = 0.2: v = 0.008; S = 0.5: v = 0.0125; S = 1: v = 0.01538; S = 2: v = 0.01739; S = 5: v = 0.01887.\nLineweaver–Burk fit: KM = 0.3, Vmax = 0.02, R² = 1.\nThe Simulate tab holds the same network over time: after a very fast transient the enzyme sits in a steady state.",
